KZ3 patch 2139 (RSX pass 131): two walker CPU cuts, each behind its own switch, both leave every byte the GPU sees unchanged.

1. LD_REFS_FAST (default on, =0 off): the compact vertex fetch's index loop (fetch_batches_hoisted, 930k indices a frame in K4, 2.2 ms a
   frame "refs" in [perf-vtx]) runs in rsx_vertex_refs_from_indices (rsx_vertex_compact.c): one call per contiguous
   index run, big-endian load, capacity reserved once, stops before a restart index so the caller records the cut
   exactly where the per-index loop did. Same refs, same order, same cuts: tools/smoke/test_vtx_refs.sh compares both
   loops on 4000 random index streams (u16/u32, restart on/off, adjacent/edge restarts, counts 0..2999).
2. LD_VTX_CACHE_SLOTS=N (power of two, 1024..4194304, default 16384): capacity of the draw-level vertex cache table
   (ld_vc_entry, two ways per set). K4 evicts ~300 entries a frame at 16384 slots, so keys that return after a turn are
   gone. The cache validates every hit as before; only the table size changes.
Defaults: see the RE notes "Pass 131".
